[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Dimensionally Scaled Newton Globalization

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NEWTON-MERIT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Frozen dimensional line-search weights
STATEMENT: >>>
While linear voltage-defined branch constraints violate their existing strict dimensional tolerance, DC and backward-Euler Newton backtracking shall compare current and candidate residuals with the same row references frozen for each correction: max(abs(rhs_i), sum_j abs(J_ij)*max(abs(x_j),abs(delta_j)), dimensional absolute tolerance). Node-row references have amperes; voltage-defined branch references have volts. Progress merit is max_i abs(F_i)/reference_i. Once these constraints are feasible, backtracking shall retain the original strict scaled-residual descent; systems without voltage-defined branch rows, and systems whose branch constraints are already feasible, shall retain their original descent policy regardless of device family.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/newton.rs::line_search_references and line_search_norm, DC and backward-Euler loops. Verification: november3_feasibility_contracts threshold/common-scale checks, retained PNP source/Gmin eight-iteration fixture on both providers; november3_globalization_contracts unit SI and row-unit property checks; tests/switch_stagnation_20261103.rs; evidence/newton-merit-20261103.md. This is a bounded local policy informed by SUNDIALS/KINSOL residual scaling, not a KINSOL implementation or qualification claim. Current-state/correction magnitude avoids evaluating an overflowing full predicted state before backtracking.
<<<
